NEW_SECTION
    builds the four instances (hero, playground, gallery, feed), wires the playground (rebuild on style edits, attribute-only update plus a resize event for smallView), refresh(parent) for inserted lists, and the nine validation buttons; commented for the reader.

REASON
CLAUDE.md requires a runnable example for every module; TimeLineList had none. Built to the
example design standard on examples/shared/example.css. Verified in headless Chromium: 31 checks
at 1280px and at 375px (no page errors, every list built, no layout element swept up, slider wrap
and unwrap, presets and textarea rebuilds, destroy/rebuild, insert then refresh with per-list
colour, all 9 validation buttons, no horizontal overflow). Two problems found while building it
became documented consumer techniques. The playground list was first called "play", the page's
own grid class, and autoBuild() turned the layout <div> into a timeline. The page's readout ran
before the rebuilt instance's resize listener and showed the old layout.
